    "body": "Initial-location requests answered with the immediate previous value because the frozen historical reader offers only each head's immediate predecessor. This adds an optional outer witness that walks each named live head's validated revision chain to its genuine assertion root, offers every exact ancestor with its depth and chain class, and learns initial-versus-previous intent with a shared signed-H4 selector that otherwise defers to the unchanged parent. The field anchor gains an explicit ancestor depth, and every dependent field read and checkpoint restore revalidates the complete path. The selector's vocabulary comes from its own committed request views (identities only for words in at least two construction views); the queried owner and any competing owner enter as role sentinels rather than spellings. Historical selection, stored identities, inner parameters and shared copy/field emission remain intact.\n\nRetain `e3a906c8`: 474/474 construction targets with 3,195/3,195 preservation cases; 474/474 targets with 778/778 preservation cases on the separately frozen third draw, after both earlier draws (402/402 with 392/392 and 488/488), the twelve matched histories and the 764-row handoff population passed as development checks. Complete removal reproduces the parent on every target; immediate-previous-only admission answers none of the deeper targets; the isolated transform control leaves the parent's own count. Plain-style requests under two phrasings receive the parent emitter's owner sentence for the same exact record (398/474 and 338/402 with exact text alone), reported separately.\n\nTwo selections were rejected before this one and are preserved with their exact failures: `f0eb0e4a` regressed 32 absent-owner rows on its independent draw (recurring absent spelling exploited), and `d6144304` passed its independent draw but regressed 72 handoff-fresh rows, six matched histories and a mixed-length competing-chain sequence. Development was explicitly reopened each time; both earlier draws became open development evidence and the retained design received its own independent draw without refit or redraw.\n\nValidation executed locally:\n- Optimized offline Rust core/API/example builds; formatting and claim-wording checks.\n- 31 focused checks: ancestor, version-intent and field/dispatch unit tests, the integer-kernel guard, the actual-artifact test (eight mixed-length initial→previous→current→arithmetic conversations, 2,884 input and 698 output checkpoint positions, 24 corrupted-path restore rejections, parent equivalence across 32 disabled turns) and a zero-allocation census.\n- 1,896 actual native API completion/checkpoint checks (948 construction, 948 fresh).\n- All 72 query-owner, 216 historical and 764 handoff-fresh comparisons preserved; fourteen older behavior/control reports have zero checked differences; twelve histories and 24 word/Rust cases preserved.\n- Copy/Add and action each pass 24 ordinary and 24 stress cases; actual generated Rust compiles and executes.\n\nThe immutable evidence records 7,634.502 model seconds and 2,175.382 engineering-command seconds, with complete cumulative resource and preservation receipts: cumulative 49,978.716/51,450.000 seconds with 196.620 seconds reserved, accounted storage 44,989,382,656/46,674,374,656 bytes with 1,550,774,272 bytes after the 128 MiB margin, and five standing-authorized extensions recorded before use. Final delivery charges append locally. No unique deletion or paid external compute occurred. Queue CI statuses are compatibility acknowledgements, not tests. Full-suite, HTTP/browser/WASM and complete-path energy checks are NOT_RUN.\n\nThese are bounded authored forms with fresh spellings; general prose, reasoning/program synthesis and alpha/frontier capability remain unfinished. A root evicted from the record ring still falls back to the parent's previous-value answer rather than abstaining, and intermediate-version intent is not claimed. Next: abstention for truncated histories, then intermediate-version intent.\n\nReferences #973. The writer-context contribution obligation under #1139 remains separate and open.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
